diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2b336b4..1f53628 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -8,6 +8,18 @@ Built against a fictional company ("Northbridge Creative", a UK digital marketin
 
 **Live demo:** https://northbridge-ledger-agent.streamlit.app/ (runs against a frozen snapshot of the seeded data, since the live Xero connection needs local credentials)
 
+## Intended use and limitations
+
+**How it works and intended use:** the checks are deterministic rules plus a statistical outlier test (median/MAD); the tool does not call an LLM or any AI model. It is a demonstration of ledger reconciliation and anomaly review on fictional or vendor sandbox data. It is **not production software** and has not been validated on real books. Every flag needs a human review, and the tool does not record that review.
+
+**Known limitations** (from an assurance review of commit 9c4127a; see the review repository):
+- The 7/7 and 84/84 results use planted anomalies written to fit the rules. They test mechanics, not accuracy on real data. The dashboard's Xero score is a published constant when the private answer key is absent.
+- Context-free rules produce false positives on legitimate items (bank charges, weekend suppliers, fixed-price or large one-off bills, recurring fixed charges).
+- Rule parameters (thresholds, tolerances, windows) are fixed constants in `src/config.py` and are not approved by a control owner.
+- Data completeness is not checked against the source system; pagination was tested with mocks only.
+- Variance sentences list the largest contributors in the direction of the movement; they describe contributors, not causes.
+- Run logging is off unless `NORTHBRIDGE_RUN_LOG` points at a SQLite file.
+
 ## Screenshot
 
 ![Dashboard screenshot](dashboard/screenshots/dashboard-full.png)
